From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shelley Vohr <shelley.vohr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Mar 2024 10:47:48 +0100
Subject: refactor: expose file system access blocklist

This CL exposes the file system access blocklist publicly so that we can leverage
it in Electron and prevent drift from Chrome's blocklist. We should look for a way
to upstream this change to Chrome.

NormalizeFilePathForBlocklist(), GenerateBlockPaths() and
ShouldBlockAccessToPath() are declared as static members in the header, and
their definitions (along with the NormalizeFilePath() and
MaybeStripMacDataVolumePrefix() helpers, and the Windows-only
ContainsInvalidDNSCharacter(), IsLocalUNCServer() and MaybeIsLocalUNCPath()
helpers they use) are moved verbatim out of
chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.cc into a new
chrome_file_system_access_blocklist.cc, which Electron compiles. Electron
therefore uses Chrome's own path matcher as well as its rules, including suffix
rules such as .git/hooks, kBlockWrite handling and the local UNC path checks.
Upstream changes to the blocklist or the matcher conflict on the hunks that
remove them from chrome_file_system_access_permission_context.cc instead of
being silently dropped; when resolving such a conflict, carry the change over
into chrome_file_system_access_blocklist.cc.

As of 158.0.8118.0, chrome_file_system_access_blocklist.cc also carries the
upstream kBlockPaths additions from that version (~/.config on all platforms,
shell startup files, .git/config and .git/modules suffix rules, /dev on mac,
and ~/.local/share, ~/.fonts.conf{,.d} and ~/.pki on Linux).

As of 159.0.8129.0, it also carries the Vim startup rules (~/.vim, ~/vimfiles,
~/.vimrc, ~/_vimrc, ~/.gvimrc, ~/_gvimrc, ~/.exrc and ~/_exrc) added upstream
in that version.

